# Test fixtures are byte-exact copies of files Brauser wrote; never convert
# their line endings on checkout (Windows CI would otherwise see CRLF).
host/tests/fixtures/** -text

# The append-only logs every worker cycle and human PR touches keep both
# sides' new entries (git's built-in union driver, which needs no
# registration). It does not run in GitHub's mergeability check, which merges
# as plain text. The improvement feed avoids needing one: each entry is its
# own file under docs/improvement-feed/ (BRAUSER_IMPROVEMENT_FEED.md). The work
# queue (.beads/issues.jsonl, BOSUN_FEATURE_BACKLOG.md) is not on this branch:
# it lives on the `beads` branch, whose own .gitattributes names its
# bead-by-bead merge drivers (AGENTS.md "Work queue").
PENDING_AMOS_DOC_UPDATES.md merge=union
CookieFeature.md merge=union

# SUMMARY.md is compiled into the host as the summary prompt; its template
# delimiters are LF-only, so never let a checkout convert it to CRLF.
SUMMARY.md text eol=lf
